  "card": "Validation snapshot loading checks coins cache memory limits only every 120,000 coins, assuming typical small coins. Because coins can contain scripts up to 10,000 bytes, a snapshot file can exceed dbcache by roughly 1.2 GB before triggering a flush check, risking out-of-memory crashes on memory-constrained systems prior to hash rejection. This change triggers a cache limit check and potential disk flush whenever dynamic memory usage increases by 4 MiB since the last check. A functional test demonstrates that loading 2,000 large coins under -dbcache=4 fails without the change and passes with it.",
